DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260603
DESCRIPTION:REGISTRATION CLOSES FRIDAY\, 5/22 !\n\n \n\nClick here to acces
 s the conference schedule.\n\n \n\nBuilding on Our Foundation: From Princi
 ples to Practice \n\nFollowing our inaugural conference's resounding succe
 ss with participants from 19 Catholic institutions\, we return with deeper
  insights and practical tools as AI reshapes education at inhuman speed. S
 ince our first gathering in October of 2024\, AI has fundamentally transfo
 rmed academic landscapes—from research methodologies to student services
 \, from classroom instruction to campus operations. \n\nThis year's confer
 ence emphasizes hands-on learning and specialized application\, featuring 
 expanded workshops and targeted breakout sessions designed for your specif
 ic role and discipline\, ensuring you leave with immediately applicable st
 rategies and tools. \n\n \n\nWHAT'S NEW FOR 2026\n\nWe've designed a highl
 y curated schedule offering hands-on workshops and interactive sessions de
 signed to equip educators and leaders with practical AI strategies. Highli
 ghts include:\n\nWorkshops on ethical AI integration\, practical AI litera
 cy for non-technical audiences\, and values-driven engagement with AI tool
 s.\n\nCase studies and tutorials focused on supporting first-generation st
 udents\, building AI literacy\, and aligning institutional mission with AI
  strategy.\n\nImmersive sessions on reflective AI use\, leadership formati
 on\, and the integration of Catholic educational values in technology adop
 tion.\n\nWhether you're seeking to deepen your understanding of AI in educ
 ation or looking for actionable tools to bring back to your institution\, 
 our workshop-heavy program offers something for everyone\n\n \n\nThe Colle
 ge of Arts and Sciences and the Dundon-Berchtold Institute for Moral Forma
 tion and Applied Ethics at the University of Portland are pleased to host 
 this essential gathering. As an independently governed Catholic university
  guided by the Congregation of Holy Cross\, the University of Portland con
 tinues its mission of teaching and learning\, faith and formation\, and se
 rvice and leadership in addressing the critical intersection of technology
  and human dignity. \n\n \n\nThank you to our conference sponsors!
GEO:45.571791;-122.724529
LOCATION:University of Portland
SUMMARY:Catholic Education and Artificial Intelligence: Principled Educatio
 nal Leadership for the AI Revolution 
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.up.edu/event/catholic-education-and-artifici
 al-intelligence
CATEGORIES:Academic
CATEGORIES:Conference / Symposium
END:VEVENT
